IMPORT prelude

-- Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) -- what long service leave an employee has earned, what counts as continuous
-- employment, payment instead of leave on termination, and what is lost or kept on resigning or being dismissed.
--
-- SEAT: the employee. "What long service leave have I earned, and what do I lose on changing employer?" Every question
-- below is phrased as the employee would ask it, on facts the employee could state.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED. Who the Act applies to (s 4(1) "employee", s 4A equivalent separate entitlements); cashing out
-- (s 5); continuous employment and how its length is counted (ss 6, 6A); ordinary pay (ss 7, 7A, 7B, 7C); service
-- carried over on a transfer of business (ss 7E, 7F, 7G, 7H, with s 41 for transfers before 20 June 2022); the
-- entitlement (s 8(1), (2), (3)); taking the leave, double or half, public holidays, and payment on termination (s 9);
-- leave in advance (s 10); records the employee may inspect (s 26A); working elsewhere while on leave (s 27).
--
-- Edition: compilation including amendments to the Industrial Relations Legislation Amendment Act 2024 Pt 4 Div 3 (No.
-- 43 of 2024, in force 31 January 2025), retrieved 7 September 2026, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_48247.txt. No regulations are used: the Act sets every number encoded here (the
-- only prescribed rate, for board and lodging under s 7C(2)(b), is an input).
--
-- NOT ENCODED. The 2006 transitional rules in s 8(4)-(10) (they bite only on employees with 9 to 15 years' service
-- before 4 July 2006); the former s 6 for businesses transmitted before 20 June 2022 (s 41: the encoding says so
-- rather than answering); the s 7(3) rate for leave postponed by agreement; the employer's record-keeping duties
-- (s 26) beyond the employee's right to see them; the transfer of records between employers (s 7I); the industrial
-- magistrate's court, inspectors, representation and regulations (ss 11, 12, 37-39: machinery). Whether an award,
-- agreement or other law gives an "at least equivalent" entitlement (s 4A(4)) is a judgment, asked as a fact. Whether
-- someone is an employee at all (the IR Act ss 7A, 7B tests the s 4(1) note points to) is asked as a fact.
--
-- BASELINE. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the individual's seat with the design defaults ruled on
-- 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice.
-- See NOTES.md.

§ `Long Service Leave Act 1958 -- the employee's questions`

§§ `s 4A -- does the Act apply to me`

-- s 4(1): "employee" means a person employed "to do work for hire or reward, including as an apprentice", and
-- "includes a casual or seasonal employee".
-- s 4A(4): "This Act does not apply to an employee who has a separate LSL entitlement ... that is at least equivalent to
-- the entitlement to WA LSL". s 4A(3): "a payment (whether in the form of a loading, other additional incremental
-- payment or otherwise) instead of an entitlement ... is not a separate LSL entitlement".
@export Does the WA Long Service Leave Act apply to me (ss 4, 4A)?
GIVEN `I am an employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are employed to do work for hire or reward (apprentices, casuals and seasonal workers included)
      `my award, agreement or another law gives me long service leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an award, industrial agreement, employer-employee agreement or another Australian law gives you long service leave and payment instead of it on termination
      `what I get instead is only a loading or extra payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what you get in place of long service leave is only a loading or other extra payment in your pay
      `if that entitlement is at least equivalent to the Act's` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that other entitlement is at least as good as the Act's, both to take leave and to be paid out on termination (a judgment: a court decides it if disputed)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Act apply to me` IF
        `I am an employee`
    AND (NOT (    `my award, agreement or another law gives me long service leave`
              AND (NOT `what I get instead is only a loading or extra payment`)
              AND `if that entitlement is at least equivalent to the Act's`))

§§ `ss 6, 6A -- what counts as continuous employment`

-- s 6(1): continuous employment "includes" an absence on annual leave, sick or carer's leave, long service leave,
-- parental leave, compassionate or bereavement leave, family and domestic violence leave, public holidays, or "any
-- other form of leave provided as part of the employee's employment", "whether paid or unpaid and irrespective of the
-- duration". s 6(2): it also includes (a) a period after a termination by the employer "made with the intention of
-- avoiding" long service leave or annual leave obligations; (b) service in the Commonwealth forces other than the
-- Permanent Forces, if the employee "resumes employment ... as soon as practicable". s 6(3): employment is continuous
-- "despite" (a) an absence the employer authorises; (b) a stand-down under an award, agreement or the Fair Work Act 2009;
-- (c) an industrial dispute "if the employee returns to work in accordance with the terms of settlement"; (d) a
-- reasonable absence on union business after leave was requested and refused; (e) any other absence "unless the
-- employer gives, during or within 14 days after the absence, written notice ... that the continuity ... has been
-- broken". s 6(4): despite a termination by the employer if re-employed within 2 months, or within 6 months if the
-- ground was "slackness of trade". s 6(5): a casual or seasonal employee keeps continuity through absences under the
-- terms of the employment, seasonal absences, and absences after which there is "a reasonable expectation of returning".
DECLARE Absence IS ONE OF
    `leave of a kind listed in s 6(1)`
    `a dismissal by my employer`
    `service in the defence force Reserves`
    `an absence my employer authorised`
    `a stand-down under an award, agreement or the Fair Work Act`
    `an absence in an industrial dispute`
    `union business after leave was refused`
    `a gap between casual or seasonal engagements`
    `some other absence`
    `my resignation`

DECLARE AbsenceFacts HAS
    `the absence` IS AN Absence
    `it was paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am a casual or seasonal employee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I came back as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I returned on the terms that settled the dispute` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my employer gave written notice within 14 days that continuity was broken` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months until my employer re-employed me` IS A NUMBER
    `the dismissal was for slackness of trade` IS A BOOLEAN
    `if the dismissal was made to avoid long service leave or annual leave` IS A BOOLEAN

-- READING (an inference): a resignation is not an "absence" in s 6, and no subsection preserves continuity through it,
-- so it ends the employment; s 6(4) re-employment saves only a termination "by the employer".
@export Is my employment still continuous after this absence (s 6)?
GIVEN `the facts` IS AN AbsenceFacts @desc What the absence was and what happened around it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employment still continuous` IF
    CONSIDER `the facts`'s `the absence`
    WHEN `leave of a kind listed in s 6(1)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a dismissal by my employer` THEN
        IF `the facts`'s `if the dismissal was made to avoid long service leave or annual leave`
        THEN TRUE
        ELSE IF `the facts`'s `the dismissal was for slackness of trade`
             THEN `the facts`'s `months until my employer re-employed me` AT MOST 6
             ELSE `the facts`'s `months until my employer re-employed me` AT MOST 2
    WHEN `service in the defence force Reserves` THEN `the facts`'s `I came back as soon as practicable`
    WHEN `an absence my employer authorised` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a stand-down under an award, agreement or the Fair Work Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an absence in an industrial dispute` THEN `the facts`'s `I returned on the terms that settled the dispute`
    WHEN `union business after leave was refused` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a gap between casual or seasonal engagements` THEN
        `the facts`'s `I am a casual or seasonal employee`
        OR (NOT `the facts`'s `my employer gave written notice within 14 days that continuity was broken`)
    WHEN `some other absence` THEN (NOT `the facts`'s `my employer gave written notice within 14 days that continuity was broken`)
    WHEN `my resignation` THEN FALSE

-- s 6A(1): counted -- (a) s 6(1) leave "for which the employee has received payment"; (b) a s 6(2) absence; (c) a
-- s 6(5) casual or seasonal absence. s 6A(2): not counted -- (a) unpaid s 6(1) leave; (b) a s 6(3) absence; (c) the gap
-- between termination and re-employment under s 6(4).
@export Does this absence count towards the length of my continuous employment (s 6A)?
GIVEN `the facts` IS AN AbsenceFacts @desc What the absence was and what happened around it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this period count towards my service` IF
        `Is my employment still continuous` `the facts`
    AND (CONSIDER `the facts`'s `the absence`
         WHEN `leave of a kind listed in s 6(1)` THEN `the facts`'s `it was paid`
         WHEN `a dismissal by my employer` THEN `the facts`'s `if the dismissal was made to avoid long service leave or annual leave`
         WHEN `service in the defence force Reserves` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a gap between casual or seasonal engagements` THEN `the facts`'s `I am a casual or seasonal employee`
         OTHERWISE FALSE)

-- s 6(7): "If an employee enters into a contract of employment with an employer within 52 weeks after completing an
-- apprenticeship with the employer, the period of apprenticeship is taken to be a part of the employee's continuous
-- employment". s 6A(2)(d): the gap between the two is not counted.
@export Does my apprenticeship count towards my long service leave with this employer (s 6(7))?
GIVEN `I did my apprenticeship with this employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the apprenticeship was with the same employer you now work for
      `weeks from finishing it to my new contract` IS A NUMBER @desc Weeks between completing the apprenticeship and entering your contract of employment with that employer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my apprenticeship count` IF
        `I did my apprenticeship with this employer`
    AND `weeks from finishing it to my new contract` AT MOST 52

§§ `ss 7E-7H, 41 -- does my service follow me to a new employer`

-- s 7E: a transfer of business needs (a) the employment with the old employer to have terminated; (b) "within 3 months
-- after the termination, the employee becomes employed by the new employer"; (c) the work is "the same, or substantially
-- the same"; (d) a connection between the employers. s 7G: a connection is (1) the new employer owns or uses, under an
-- arrangement, assets of the old employer relating to the work; (2) the old employer outsourced the work to the new;
-- (3) the new employer ends its outsourcing to the old; (4) the new employer is a related body corporate of the old.
-- s 7H: then "employment before and after the transfer is taken to be a single period of continuous employment" and the
-- new employer "is taken to have been the transferring employee's sole employer for the entire period".
-- s 8(1): leave is earned "with the same employer". Without a transfer, service with a new employer starts from zero.
-- s 41: for a "transmission" of business before the IRLA 2021 s 84 commencement day (20 June 2022), the former ss 6 and
-- 8 continue and Division 3 does not apply.
DECLARE Connection IS ONE OF
    `the new employer took over assets used in my work under an arrangement`
    `my old employer outsourced my work to the new employer`
    `the new employer brought back work it had outsourced to my old employer`
    `the new employer is a related body corporate of my old employer`
    `no connection between the employers`

DECLARE ChangeOfEmployer HAS
    `my employment with the old employer ended` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months until the new employer employed me` IS A NUMBER
    `my work is the same or substantially the same` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the connection` IS A Connection
    `the business was transmitted before 20 June 2022` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE ServiceOutcome IS ONE OF
    `my service carries over to the new employer`
    `my service with the new employer starts from zero`
    `the former s 6 decides, as the business was transmitted before 20 June 2022`

@export When I change employer, does my service carry over for long service leave (ss 7E-7H, 8(1), 41)?
GIVEN `the change` IS A ChangeOfEmployer @desc How you moved from the old employer to the new one
GIVETH A ServiceOutcome
DECIDE `Does my service carry over` IS
    IF `the change`'s `the business was transmitted before 20 June 2022`
    THEN `the former s 6 decides, as the business was transmitted before 20 June 2022`
    ELSE IF     `the change`'s `my employment with the old employer ended`
            AND `the change`'s `months until the new employer employed me` AT MOST 3
            AND `the change`'s `my work is the same or substantially the same`
            AND (NOT (`the change`'s `the connection` EQUALS `no connection between the employers`))
         THEN `my service carries over to the new employer`
         ELSE `my service with the new employer starts from zero`

§§ `s 8 -- how much long service leave have I earned`

-- s 8(2): "An employee who has completed at least 10 years of continuous employment is entitled ... (a) in respect of
-- 10 years so completed, 8 2/3 weeks; (b) in respect of each 5 years' continuous employment so completed after such 10
-- years, 4 1/3 weeks". 8 2/3 weeks is 26/3; 4 1/3 weeks is 13/3.
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `weeks for ten years` IS 26 DIVIDED BY 3

GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `weeks for each further five years` IS 13 DIVIDED BY 3

GIVEN `years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `completed five-year blocks after ten` IS
    IF `years` LESS THAN 10 THEN 0 ELSE TRUNC ((`years` MINUS 10) DIVIDED BY 5) 0

@export How many weeks of long service leave have I earned so far while still employed (s 8(2)(a), (b))?
GIVEN `years of continuous employment` IS A NUMBER @desc Your years of continuous employment with this employer, counted under s 6A (unpaid leave left out)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of long service leave have I earned` IS
    IF `years of continuous employment` LESS THAN 10
    THEN 0
    ELSE     `weeks for ten years`
        PLUS `weeks for each further five years` TIMES `completed five-year blocks after ten` `years of continuous employment`

-- s 8(2)(c): on termination "by the employee's death" or "in any circumstances otherwise than by the employer for
-- serious misconduct", "in respect of the number of years of such continuous employment completed since the employee
-- last became entitled ... a proportionate amount on the basis of 8 2/3 weeks for 10 years". READING: "years ...
-- completed" is whole years since the last 10- or 5-year mark.
-- s 8(3): with "at least 7 years but less than 10 years" and the same kinds of termination, "a proportionate amount on
-- the basis of 8 2/3 weeks for 10 years of such continuous employment". READING (an inference): proportionate to the
-- whole length of continuous employment, part years included, as s 8(3) does not say "years completed".
-- s 9(2): an employee entitled under s 8(2) or (3) whose employment ends before all the leave is taken "is taken to have
-- commenced long service leave on the day of termination", and s 9(2A) the employer "must pay the full amount" that day.
-- So leave already accrued under s 8(2)(a), (b) is paid out even on a dismissal for serious misconduct.
DECLARE Termination IS ONE OF
    `I resigned`
    `my employer dismissed me for serious misconduct`
    `my employer dismissed me for another reason`
    `my job was made redundant`
    `I died`

GIVEN `how it ended` IS A Termination
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the pro rata entitlement is lost` IF
    `how it ended` EQUALS `my employer dismissed me for serious misconduct`

GIVEN `years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `whole years since I last became entitled` IS
    TRUNC (`years` MINUS 10 MINUS 5 TIMES `completed five-year blocks after ten` `years`) 0

@export How many weeks of long service leave am I entitled to when my employment ends, before any leave taken (s 8(2), (3))?
GIVEN `years of continuous employment` IS A NUMBER @desc Your years of continuous employment with this employer, counted under s 6A (unpaid leave left out)
      `how it ended` IS A Termination @desc How the employment ended
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks am I entitled to on termination` IS
    IF `years of continuous employment` LESS THAN 7
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `years of continuous employment` LESS THAN 10
         THEN IF `the pro rata entitlement is lost` `how it ended`
              THEN 0
              ELSE `weeks for ten years` TIMES `years of continuous employment` DIVIDED BY 10
         ELSE     `How many weeks of long service leave have I earned` `years of continuous employment`
             PLUS (IF `the pro rata entitlement is lost` `how it ended`
                   THEN 0
                   ELSE `weeks for ten years` TIMES `whole years since I last became entitled` `years of continuous employment` DIVIDED BY 10)

@export How many weeks of long service leave must I be paid out when my employment ends (ss 8, 9(2), 9(2A))?
GIVEN `years of continuous employment` IS A NUMBER @desc Your years of continuous employment with this employer, counted under s 6A (unpaid leave left out)
      `how it ended` IS A Termination @desc How the employment ended
      `weeks of long service leave already taken` IS A NUMBER @desc Weeks of long service leave you have already taken or been paid for with this employer
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks must I be paid out` IS
    max 0 (`How many weeks am I entitled to on termination` `years of continuous employment` `how it ended` MINUS `weeks of long service leave already taken`)

§§ `ss 7, 7A, 7B, 7C -- what is my ordinary pay`

-- s 7(1): "remuneration for the employee's normal weekly number of hours of work calculated on the ordinary time rate
-- of pay" when the leave starts; (2) where hours varied, "the average weekly hours worked". s 7(4): paid "wholly or
-- partly by results", "average weekly rate of pay earned over a period totalling 365 days". s 7A: ordinary pay "does
-- not include shift premiums, overtime, penalty rates, allowances or any similar payments". s 7B: "A casual employee's
-- ordinary pay includes any casual loading". s 7C: it includes "the cash value of board and lodging" the employer
-- provides but which is not taken during the leave.
DECLARE PayFacts HAS
    `I am paid wholly or partly by results` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my average weekly pay over the last 365 days` IS A NUMBER
    `my normal weekly hours` IS A NUMBER
    `my ordinary hourly rate` IS A NUMBER
    `my casual loading as a fraction` IS A NUMBER
    `weekly cash value of board and lodging I will not take` IS A NUMBER

@export What is my weekly ordinary pay for long service leave, in dollars (ss 7, 7A, 7B, 7C)?
GIVEN `my pay` IS A PayFacts @desc How you are paid (leave out overtime, shift premiums, penalty rates and allowances)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my weekly ordinary pay` IS
        (IF `my pay`'s `I am paid wholly or partly by results`
         THEN `my pay`'s `my average weekly pay over the last 365 days`
         ELSE `my pay`'s `my normal weekly hours` TIMES `my pay`'s `my ordinary hourly rate` TIMES (1 PLUS `my pay`'s `my casual loading as a fraction`))
    PLUS `my pay`'s `weekly cash value of board and lodging I will not take`

@export How much must I be paid for long service leave when my employment ends, in dollars (ss 8, 9(2A))?
GIVEN `years of continuous employment` IS A NUMBER @desc Your years of continuous employment with this employer, counted under s 6A
      `how it ended` IS A Termination @desc How the employment ended
      `weeks of long service leave already taken` IS A NUMBER @desc Weeks of long service leave already taken or paid with this employer
      `my weekly ordinary pay` IS A NUMBER @desc Your weekly ordinary pay in dollars (s 7)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much must I be paid out` IS
    `How many weeks must I be paid out` `years of continuous employment` `how it ended` `weeks of long service leave already taken`
        TIMES `my weekly ordinary pay`

§§ `s 9 -- taking the leave`

-- s 9(1AA): employee and employer "may agree when the employee will take long service leave". s 9(1a): without
-- agreement, "the employer is not to refuse the employee taking, at any time suitable to the employee, any period of
-- long service leave to which the employee became entitled more than 12 months before that time"; (1b) the employee
-- must give "at least 2 weeks' notice".
@export May I take my long service leave at a time I choose, without my employer's agreement (s 9(1a), (1b))?
GIVEN `my employer and I have agreed when I take it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your employer have already agreed when you will take the leave
      `months since I became entitled to it` IS A NUMBER @desc Months since you became entitled to this period of leave
      `weeks of notice I give` IS A NUMBER @desc Weeks of notice you give your employer of the period you intend to take
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I take my leave when I choose` IF
        (NOT `my employer and I have agreed when I take it`)
    AND `months since I became entitled to it` GREATER THAN 12
    AND `weeks of notice I give` AT LEAST 2

-- s 9(1C): the employee "may request" leave "twice as long" at "half the employee's ordinary pay"; s 9(1D): "half as
-- long" at "twice the employee's ordinary pay". READING: these are requests; the Act does not oblige the employer to
-- grant them. The functions answer what the leave looks like if the request is granted.
DECLARE LeaveMode IS ONE OF
    `at full pay`
    `twice as long at half pay`
    `half as long at double pay`

@export If my request is granted, how many weeks of leave do I get (s 9(1C), (1D))?
GIVEN `weeks of leave` IS A NUMBER @desc Weeks of long service leave you are entitled to at full pay
      `the mode` IS A LeaveMode @desc Full pay, twice as long at half pay, or half as long at double pay
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of leave if granted` IS
    CONSIDER `the mode`
    WHEN `at full pay` THEN `weeks of leave`
    WHEN `twice as long at half pay` THEN `weeks of leave` TIMES 2
    WHEN `half as long at double pay` THEN `weeks of leave` DIVIDED BY 2

@export If my request is granted, what fraction of my ordinary pay am I paid during the leave (s 9(1C), (1D))?
GIVEN `the mode` IS A LeaveMode @desc Full pay, twice as long at half pay, or half as long at double pay
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What fraction of my ordinary pay during leave` IS
    CONSIDER `the mode`
    WHEN `at full pay` THEN 1
    WHEN `twice as long at half pay` THEN 1 DIVIDED BY 2
    WHEN `half as long at double pay` THEN 2

-- s 9(3): paid "at the time payment is made in the normal course of the employment, unless (a) the employee requests in
-- writing to be paid before the period of leave commences, in which case the employee is to be so paid".
@export Must I be paid for my long service leave before it starts (s 9(3))?
GIVEN `I asked in writing to be paid before the leave starts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you asked your employer in writing to be paid before the leave begins
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be paid before my leave starts` IF
    `I asked in writing to be paid before the leave starts`

-- s 9(4): for leave under s 8(2)(a) or (b), "the period of long service leave is increased by one day for each such
-- public holiday" falling in it to which the employee is otherwise entitled.
@export How many days longer is my long service leave because of public holidays (s 9(4))?
GIVEN `public holidays during my leave that I would otherwise get` IS A NUMBER @desc Public holidays falling in your leave to which your conditions of employment otherwise entitle you
      `the leave is taken under s 8(2)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this is leave taken while employed after 10 (or 15, 20 ...) years, not leave paid out on termination
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days longer is my leave` IS
    IF `the leave is taken under s 8(2)(a) or (b)`
    THEN `public holidays during my leave that I would otherwise get`
    ELSE 0

§§ `s 5 -- cashing out`

-- s 5(1): employer and employee "may agree that the employee may forgo" leave under s 8(2)(a) or (b) if (a) "the
-- employee is given an adequate benefit instead" and (b) "the agreement is in writing, signed by the employer and
-- employee". (2): not adequate "unless the employee is paid at least the amount of ordinary pay the employee would have
-- received had the employee taken the long service leave". (3): no agreement "before the employee's entitlement to long
-- service leave has accrued".
@export Is my agreement to cash out long service leave valid (s 5)?
GIVEN `the leave has already accrued under s 8(2)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the leave being cashed out had already accrued (after 10, 15, 20 ... years) when you agreed
      `the agreement is in writing signed by both of us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement is in writing and signed by you and your employer
      `the amount I am paid` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars you are paid instead of the leave
      `ordinary pay I would have received for that leave` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars of ordinary pay you would have received had you taken the leave
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my cash-out agreement valid` IF
        `the leave has already accrued under s 8(2)(a) or (b)`
    AND `the agreement is in writing signed by both of us`
    AND `the amount I am paid` AT LEAST `ordinary pay I would have received for that leave`

§§ `s 10 -- leave taken in advance`

-- s 10(1): leave may be allowed by agreement "before the right has accrued due". (2): if the employment then ends, "the
-- employer may deduct from whatever remuneration is payable upon the termination ... such amount as represents payment
-- for any period" of leave to which the employee "was not at the date of termination ... entitled".
@export How many weeks of leave taken in advance can my employer recover from my final pay (s 10(2))?
GIVEN `weeks of leave I took` IS A NUMBER @desc Weeks of long service leave you have taken, including any taken in advance
      `weeks I was entitled to when my employment ended` IS A NUMBER @desc Weeks of long service leave you were entitled to on the day the employment ended (s 8)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks can my employer deduct` IS
    max 0 (`weeks of leave I took` MINUS `weeks I was entitled to when my employment ended`)

§§ `s 27 -- working elsewhere while on leave`

-- s 27(1): the employee "must not, during any period when the employee is on long service leave, engage in any
-- employment for reward in substitution for the employment from which the employee is on leave". (2): if so, the
-- employee "forfeits the right to leave in respect of the unexpired period", and the employer may withhold further
-- payment and "reclaim any payments already made". (3): not for leave taken to commence on termination under s 9(2).
@export Do I forfeit the rest of my long service leave by working for someone else during it (s 27)?
GIVEN `I worked for reward in place of my job during the leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, while on long service leave, you took paid work in substitution for the job you are on leave from
      `this is leave I was taken to start on termination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this is the leave you are treated as starting on the day your employment ended (s 9(2))
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I forfeit the rest of my leave` IF
        `I worked for reward in place of my job during the leave`
    AND (NOT `this is leave I was taken to start on termination`)

§§ `s 26A -- seeing my records`

-- s 26A(1): on "request in writing by a relevant person" the employer "must" produce and let the person inspect the
-- records. (2): relevant persons include "the employee or a person authorised in writing by the employee". (3)(a): the
-- duty continues while the record must be kept, which s 26(2)(b) makes "during the employment ... and for not less than
-- 7 years after that"; (b) "is not affected by the fact that the employee is no longer employed"; (d) must be met "not
-- later than the end of the next pay period after the request". A contravention is a civil penalty provision, not an
-- offence (s 26A(1a)).
@export Must my employer let me see my long service leave records (s 26A)?
GIVEN `I or someone I authorised in writing asked in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, or a person you authorised in writing, asked the employer in writing
      `years since my employment ended` IS A NUMBER @desc Years since your employment with that employer ended (0 if you still work there)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my employer let me see my records` IF
        `I or someone I authorised in writing asked in writing`
    AND `years since my employment ended` AT MOST 7

@export By when must my employer let me see my records (s 26A(3)(d))?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `By when must I be shown my records` IS "by the end of the next pay period after the request"
